  "objects": {

            #ENTRANCE
    "object.front_door.name": "Front Door",
    "object.front_door.description":["It’s a heavy looking door. Strange symbols are carved into the frame."],

    "object.decorations.name":"Decorations",
    "object.decorations.description":["Besides the emblems, you see various tapestries depicting knights fighting mythical beasts, some portraits of kings, queens, and other figures.",
      "You don’t recognise any of these people, but they somehow feel familiar. You imagine these kind of portraits and scenes all resemble each other in some way."
      ],

    "object.tapestry.name":"Tapestry",
    "object.tapestry.description": [ "The heavy fabric covers a considerable portion of the wall. You see an intricated collection of scenes, objects and symbols woven into it:", 
      "at the top, a knight on their horse passing by a young man walking on a small path in the forest, the two headed in opposite directions.", 
      "From the sides of the image starts an elegant ornamental border, which frames the whole lenght, coming to a close at another scene on the bottom:", 
      "on what looks like the courtyard of a palace, two figures walk away together, their shoulders bumping.", 
      "Getting as close as you can to try and discern the middle part, you accidentally lose your balance and put your hands forward to avoid crashing into the wall.", 
      "Except. While your right hand collides with the wall beside the tapestry and stops you, the left one encounters no further resistance than the thick fabric.", 
      "It seems there’s a hollow space hidden behind it."
    ],
    
    "object.tapestry.move": [ "You carefully move the tapestry aside, expecting to find a nook protecting what hopefully was a clue on where you are or how to get out. What you find, instead, is the threshold of a room." 
    ],

    "object.merlin.name":"The Sorcerer",
    "object.merlin.description": [ "The life-sized statue is an impressive work of art. The clothes and long magic staff so intricately carved, they seemed ready to move with the slightest shift of their owner.", 
      "The young man’s features so defined and vivid, you could almost see a spark of mischief in his eyes. It’s a bit jarring, the impression it could start talking and moving at any moment."
    ],

     #FIRST INTERACTION BEFORE ARTHUR
    "object.melin.talk.1": [ "You can’t help move your hand to touch the statue, almost expecting to find fabric instead of stone.", 
      "As soon as your fingertips make contact, something surprising does happen, but it's not the texture of the clothes: the statue shifts to look in your direction and starts to talk.",
      "'Oh, you’re here? Good, how is this round going? Have you talked to my lord yet?'",
      "You remain silent, completely caught off guard by the fact that a statue just came alive before your very eyes.",
      "There’s a brief pause in which the statue waits expectently for a reply and then, somehow even more shockingly, it smirks.", 
      "‘I’ll take that as a no. Well, I fear he’s the only one who can grant you permission to leave, so you better be on your way and find him.’ "
      
    ],

    #FIRST INTERACTION BUT YOU ALREADY FOUND ARTHUR SOMEHOW
    "object.merlin.talk.2": [ "As soon as your fingertips make contact, the statue shifts to look in your direction and starts to talk.",
      "‘Oh, you’re here? Good, how is this round going? Have you talked to my lord yet?’",
      "You nod your head and he smiles, looking satisfied.",
      "‘Well, what are you here for, then? Shouldn’t you already be out?’ he smirks, the impossible sparkle in his eyes heightening like he already knows the answer."
      
    ],

    #SECOND INTERACTION (WITH SWORD, NO FLOWER)
    "object.merlin.talk.3": [ "You offer the sorcerer the sword you found, explaining what the statue of the king requested, and the sorcerer’s expression grows complicated.",
      "‘Broken? How is that even… never mind, I can indeed create another magical sword, all I need is this,’ he moves the hand holding the sword, ‘and my good friend’s firey breath’ he nods torwards the dragon head on the opposite wall.",
      "‘But. You see, swords forged with dragon fire are especially powerful, and dangerous. I cannot let it fall in the wrong hands and, even if I was willing to risk it, the Great Dragon would never accept to help.", 
      "So, I’m afraid I will need you to prove that the person that will receive it is indeed my liege. He will surely be able to provide something to attest his identity.’ With this, the statue stilled completely once again."
      
    ],

    #THIRD INTERACTION (WITH SWORD AND FLOWER)
    "object.merlin.talk.4": [ "The sorcerer comes to life and his eyebrows raise in surprise as he sees the flower in your hand.", 
      "‘That..’ his voice sounds strange ‘...will do. No one but my lord would know of the significance of the Mortaeus Flower, not enough to use it as identification anyway.’",
      "( He murmurs something to himself. You’re not able to catch the words, but by the inflection you think it might be some sort of insult. Even so, he’s shaking his head with a small smile.) ",
      "‘Alright, time to forge a sword then.' With nothing more than a look headed in its direction, the sword slides off your hip and starts to fluctuate in the space in front of the dragon head.", 
      "Then, the sorcerer starts to speak a language you don’t recognize in a guttural, deep voice. The head of the dragon comes to life. Big, golden eyes blink open as it huffs a puff of black smoke out of its nostrils.",
      "‘In need of help again, are we, young warlock?’ the dragon sounds amused, and you’re not sure why you find yourself surprised that the dragon can talk. At this point you should have expected it.", 
      "At your side, the sorcerer – warlock? – chuckles. ‘Yes, old friend. It seems our King is in need of a new sword, worthy of his old one. Will you help me?’",
      "The dragon looks displeased. ‘You know of the risks and responsibilities it comes with, are you sure of what you are asking?’ At his assent, it let out a resigned sigh.", 
      "‘Very well’ it says, and opens its mouth a bit wider. Flames envelope the floating sword as it breathes out. When it stops, the sword is alight with a mystical glow that slowly fades away.",
      "You’re so captivated by the magic display that you completely miss the few words exchanged in soft voices by the statue and the dragon, and the latter closing its eyes and still again, only coming back to your surroundings when the statue addresses you.",
      "‘You can touch it, it won’t burn.’ the statue says, and you secure it again to your side. ‘Please, make sure to keep it safe until it’s in the hands of its rightful master’ he says gravely.",
      "‘And,’ he stops and you wait for him to continue, curiosity peaking at the expression on his face.",
      "‘...if you would,’ he continues eventually ‘tell that dollophead to take care of this one. He won’t get any more. You can tell him I called him that.’ He seems happy at the thought as he shakes his head.", 
      "Then, for just a split second, a sad look crosses his face, quickly covered by a big smile as the statue bids you goodbye, and resumes his pose once again."
      
    ],

    "object.kilgharrah.name":"Great Dragon",
    "object.kilgharrah.description": ["An uncomfortably realistic mounted head of an enourmous dragon, with bronze scales. Its eyes are closed."]


          #DINING ROOM
    
    "object.table.name":"Round Table",
    "object.table.description": [ "The round table in the center of the room could easily fit more than a dozen people.", 
