                #SECRET ROOM

    "object.arthur.name":"The King",
    "object.arthur.description": ["Moving closer to the statue, you can make out more details: The long cape pinned to its shoulders, the light armour, the solid lines of its features and the crown on its head."],
    "object.arthur.examine": ["As you reach out, the statue moves, the man’s eyes lending on you. ‘Ah. Looking for the way out, I would guess, yes?’. You nod, at a loss for words. This place is so weird.",
      "‘I have what you seek, but I will have to ask a favor of you before I had it over to you. You see, I used to have a great sword with which I could face any sort of enemy.", 
      "It had been a loyal companion in many battles, but it seems to have lost its resilience, as it recently got snapped. I am in dire need of a new sword to defend myself and my kingdom. Would you help me find a valid replacement?’.", 
      "It is an easy decision to make, you don’t really have many other options. You nod, and the man looks satisfied. ‘You have my thanks, then.’ He says, stopping his motions immediately after."
    ],
    "object.arthur.conditional.examine": ["You approach the king, and he comes alive. ‘Well?’ he asks, expectantly. You explain to him what the sorcerer requested, and he actually rolls his eyes – not very “kingly” of him – as he listen.",
      "‘Of course he would make this difficult…’ he complains under his breath, bringing a hand on his chin to think. After a moment of concentration, he lights up and reaches for a satchel at his side you didn’t notice before.",
      "It’s not made of stone like the rest of the statue, but leather. Now that you watch closely, other little details seem to also have been applied to the statue in other materials, making it look all the more realistic.",
      "As you wonder the reason, he opens the satchel and gently pulls something out, resting it gently in his other open palm. ‘You can bring him this.’ he seems a bit awkward and you curiosly move a little closer to see what he found.",
      "It’s a flower. A delicate, strange, golden flower. You arch an eyebrow at the statue, and you have the feeling he is trying to look extra stoic and regal to cover for the fact that he’s actually a little embarassed.",
      "‘Go on then, take it. He will recognize it and know it can only come from me. Do be careful, please. It is incredibly difficult and very dangerous to get this flower.", 
      "And don’t get it too close to your face. The petals are poisonous, I’m not sure if the smell could do some damage as well.’",
      "You take the flower, careful not to accidentally ruin it – or inhale its smell – and turn around to make fast work of this side quest.", 
      "‘Is he...’ you think you hear from behind you, but it’s so soft you’re not really sure, and when you turn around to ask him to repeat, the statue is just a statue again."
    ],
    "object.arthur.final.examine": ["“You retrieve the newly magically-forged sword from your side to present it to the king. He takes it and turns it around in his hand, studying it under the soft lights and trying a couple of moves to get a feeling of it, before nodding, appeased.",
      "His eyes land on you. ‘You did well on this quest my friend. I thank you for your help. As promised, this is your reward.’ There is a metal jingle coming from his belt, where he extricates a large ring filled with keys.",
      "He takes one off and offers it to you. You take it esitantly. ‘There’s a door at the very end of the hallway past the library. This key will open it. Farewell, my friend, take good care of yourself.’ ",
      "He smiles minutely and offers you his arm in a final greeting. You grip his forearm and he does the same. You nod to each other. You’re about to go, when you remember the message the sorcerer asked you to deliever.",
      "You’re a bit worried the king will take offence at being called a ‘dollophead’, but he starts to laugh surprised and evidently amused. He shakes his head and thanks you again.",
      "Then, slowly, the king resumes his guarding stance, the shadow of a private smile resting on the stone face the only clue anything at all really happened, and you walk away."
    ],


